<script>
/* ==================================================================
   VN DOCUMENT VIEWER — portable core
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   The patient's Documents screen (folder tree + list → full-modal
   viewer) and a widget search, with NO knowledge of the page it runs
   in. The host decides where the modal sits and where the search goes;
   the core only draws them and keeps their state.

     VDocs.init({
       data:   { folders:[…], kids:Set, docs:{folder:[{f,svc,cr,kb,img?,by?,pages()}]} },
       folder: 'Visit Note',                     first folder shown
       widgets: () => [{id, t, m, here}],        what the search lists
       go:     id => {…},                        navigate to a widget
       onOpen: side => {…}, onClose: () => {…},  placement is the host's job
       note:   text => html                      optional design-note badge
     })
     VDocs.open('left'|'right') · VDocs.close() · VDocs.modal · VDocs.search
     VDocs.state() · VDocs.toast(html) · VDocs.fit()   (re-fit zoom after a resize)

   Styles: vndocs.core.css — every selector .vd-* / #vd* / .vdp-*, and
   it must be injected as <style id="vdCss"> so "open in new tab" can
